WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:14.721
On a clear sunny morning, two people walked up a narrow mountain path.

2
00:00:15.221 --> 00:00:20.444
Detie, a tall, strong-looking young woman, was leading a girl named Heidi by the hand.

3
00:00:21.224 --> 00:00:24.645
Heidi had a heart-shaped face and short, curly brown hair.

4
00:00:25.806 --> 00:00:28.327
Detie, who looked after Heidi, was her aunt.

5
00:00:29.147 --> 00:00:32.801
She had accepted a new job in Frankfurt and could not take Heidi with her.

6
00:00:33.521 --> 00:00:36.522
She had decided to take Heidi to live with Heidi's grandfather.

7
00:00:37.463 --> 00:00:42.145
Grandfather lived high on the mountain where the flowers and grass grew wild among the rocks.

8
00:00:42.905 --> 00:00:46.747
As she climbed, Heidi could smell the short grasses and mountain plants.

9
00:00:47.307 --> 00:00:53.069
High above her, on the steep slope just below the mountaintop, she could see a tiny herd of

10
00:00:53.129 --> 00:00:59.572
goats. Against the side of Grandfather's hut, looking down toward the valley, was Grandfather's chair.

11
00:01:00.224 --> 00:01:04.268
When they came over the rise, Heidi saw him sitting there with his pipe in his mouth.

12
00:01:05.549 --> 00:01:08.812
"I wish you good day," said Detie, as she walked toward him.

13
00:01:09.352 --> 00:01:10.913
"I have brought you your granddaughter.

14
00:01:11.294 --> 00:01:12.715
You will hardly recognize her.

15
00:01:13.075 --> 00:01:15.297
You haven't seen her since she was one year old."

16
00:01:16.358 --> 00:01:22.624
While frowning at Heidi, the old man asked rudely, "And why have you brought the child up here

17
00:01:22.684 --> 00:01:23.384
to see me?"

18
00:01:23.404 --> 00:01:27.788
"Because she is going to live with you," said Detie.

19
00:01:27.808 --> 00:01:30.969
"I have done my duty looking after her since her parents died.

20
00:01:31.489 --> 00:01:33.470
Now it is your turn to do your duty."

21
00:01:33.490 --> 00:01:36.070
"So, that's it, is it?"

22
00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:39.731
said the old man, as he looked at Detie with a flash in his eye.

23
00:01:39.751 --> 00:01:45.533
"And what am I supposed to do when she starts to cry and whine because she misses you?"

24
00:01:45.553 --> 00:01:48.894
"That's your business," replied Detie.

25
00:01:49.474 --> 00:01:51.574
"She was left with me when she was a baby.

26
00:01:51.594 --> 00:01:54.095
I have put up with her for five years.

27
00:01:54.695 --> 00:01:57.276
If you cannot arrange to keep her, do what you want with her.

28
00:01:57.744 --> 00:02:01.027
But remember you will be responsible if any harm comes to her."

29
00:02:01.728 --> 00:02:03.809
Detie was suddenly feeling hot and irritable.

30
00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:07.753
She felt a little guilty about leaving Heidi alone with her grandfather.

31
00:02:08.333 --> 00:02:12.757
With a stern loud voice, Grandfather replied, "Go away right now!

32
00:02:13.357 --> 00:02:16.920
I don't want to see your face again anytime soon!"

33
00:02:18.081 --> 00:02:22.045
Detie did not wait to be told twice, and with a quick "Good-bye!"

34
00:02:22.505 --> 00:02:25.548
to Heidi, she turned and ran down the mountain.

35
00:02:26.388 --> 00:02:31.432
When Detie reached Dorfli, the village in the valley below, the women began to criticize her.

36
00:02:32.833 --> 00:02:36.456
They had seen Detie take Heidi up the mountain and knew what she had done.

37
00:02:37.037 --> 00:02:40.359
One woman cried out, "How could you do such a thing?"

38
00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:46.104
Another said, "To think of leaving a helpless little girl up there with such a grumpy man!"

39
00:02:47.385 --> 00:02:49.787
Detie hurried through the village as quickly as she could.

40
00:02:50.207 --> 00:02:54.871
She promised herself that, when she had plenty of money from her new job, she would do something

41
00:02:54.931 --> 00:02:55.572
good for Heidi.

42
00:02:56.904 --> 00:02:59.547
After Detie left, Heidi decided to explore.

43
00:03:00.007 --> 00:03:03.410
She found a shed built against the hut, but inside it was empty.

44
00:03:04.511 --> 00:03:06.633
Behind the hut, she discovered some fir trees.

45
00:03:07.173 --> 00:03:09.435
Their large branches grew in curious twists.

46
00:03:10.336 --> 00:03:15.180
A strong breeze was blowing, and it made a rushing sound in the branches that sounded like music.

47
00:03:15.861 --> 00:03:18.843
Heidi twirled and jumped and felt the cool wind on her cheeks.

48
00:03:19.424 --> 00:03:23.147
She was enjoying herself so much she almost forgot about her grandfather.
